-- Migration 13: the instrument's own words, persisted.
--
-- The console log was the only record of what the instrument said while a session ran, and it lived
-- in a StateFlow capped at 200 lines that died with the process. The diagnosis of walk B's lost mesh
-- (2026-08-19) came from the sidecar's terse `lifecycle.events`; the sentence that actually explained
-- it — "mesh export refused: ARKit holds no mesh anchors" with everything the instrument said around
-- it — was on a screen nobody was reading and gone at close.
--
-- So log lines are now a session stream like any other: written as they are said, on the same
-- `mono_ns` clock, uploaded as `log.tsv` with the artefacts. A session the OS kills keeps every line
-- it managed to say, which is precisely the session whose log matters.
--
-- Purely additive. A device upgrading from schema 13 gains one empty table, and every existing
-- session reads as a session whose instrument said nothing that survived — which is what happened.
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS InstrumentLogRecord (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    sessionId TEXT NOT NULL,
    monoNs INTEGER NOT NULL,
    wallMs INTEGER NOT NULL,
    message TEXT NOT NULL
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_instrument_log_session ON InstrumentLogRecord(sessionId, monoNs);
